## Key Implementation Notes

- use tauri::Manager; must be explicitly imported in Rust for get_webview_window to resolve
- Global hotkey uses two-window pattern: overlay is persistent + hidden by default, never re-created
- From JS side: getCurrentWebviewWindow().hide() (Tauri 2.0 WebviewWindow API) dismisses overlay
- notify crate has FSEvents debouncing quirks on macOS — use ~500ms debounce window
- SQLite schema is locked early — migrations are painful, get the schema right first
- Rust Tauri commands stay thin — they are the API boundary, keep signatures clean
- Claude API calls accept mcp_servers array for future Tier 3 connector passthrough
- File content is never sent to Claude without explicit user opt-in (privacy default)
- Confidence threshold for auto-move vs pending inbox: tune with real usage, start conservative
- macOS transparency requires macOSPrivateApi in tauri.conf.json and macos-private-api Cargo feature

